This is a miscompilation bug in InstCombine.
Issue title: [RISC-V] Miscompile using rv64gcv
Detailed information:
BUG TYPE:
    miscompilation

VERIFICATION RESULT:
    Invalid refinement in @pr126974 -- Value mismatch

VIOLATED PROPERTY:
    return-value equality

SOURCE (pre-transformation IR):
define i1 @pr126974(i8 %x) {
entry:
  %cond = icmp sgt i8 %x, -2
  br i1 %cond, label %if.then, label %if.else

if.then:                                          ; preds = %entry
  %umax = call i8 @llvm.umax.i8(i8 %x, i8 -46)
  %cmp = icmp samesign ult i8 %umax, -32
  ret i1 %cmp

if.else:                                          ; preds = %entry
  ret i1 false
}

; Function Attrs: nocallback nosync nounwind speculatable willreturn memory(none)
declare i8 @llvm.umax.i8(i8, i8) #0

attributes #0 = { nocallback nosync nounwind speculatable willreturn memory(none) }

TARGET (post-transformation IR):
; ModuleID = '<stdin>'
source_filename = "<stdin>"

define i1 @pr126974(i8 %x) {
entry:
  %cond = icmp sgt i8 %x, -2
  br i1 %cond, label %if.then, label %if.else

if.then:                                          ; preds = %entry
  ret i1 false

if.else:                                          ; preds = %entry
  ret i1 false
}

; Function Attrs: nocallback nosync nounwind speculatable willreturn memory(none)
declare i8 @llvm.umax.i8(i8, i8) #0

attributes #0 = { nocallback nosync nounwind speculatable willreturn memory(none) }

WHAT THE TRANSFORMATION CHANGED:
  only in source:
    %umax: %umax = call i8 @llvm.umax.i8(i8 %x, i8 -46)
    %cmp: %cmp = icmp samesign ult i8 %umax, -32

CRITICAL VALUES:
    %cmp
    %umax

DEPENDENCY CHAIN (source):
    %cond = icmp sgt i8 %x, -2
    %umax = call i8 @llvm.umax.i8(i8 %x, i8 -46)
    %cmp = icmp samesign ult i8 %umax, -32

CONTROL FLOW (blocks entered by the failing execution):
    %if.then

COUNTEREXAMPLE INPUT:
    i8 %x = #x00 (0)

DIVERGENCE (source vs target on that input):
    (none)

INTERPRETATION:
    A transformation must preserve the returned value for every input on which the source is well-defined.
    On the input above the source yields #x1 (1) while the target yields #x0 (0).

